[ti:Afterglow]
[00:09.96][Verse]
[00:10.04]Room key sleeping by the ashtray
[00:14.60]Blue light crawling up the wall
[00:18.92]The old TV forgets its weather
[00:23.44]A silent taxi waits below
[00:28.16]Red heels shine beside the doorway
[00:32.68]Half a drink has lost its gold
[00:37.20]Someone laughs behind the velvet
[00:41.72]Like a story badly told
[00:45.48]The elevator sings my floor
[00:49.48]The phone keeps breathing in the dark
[00:54.24]I let the curtain hide the morning
[00:58.48]And leave the window slightly ajar
[01:03.20][Chorus]
[01:03.28]Afterglow, afterglow
[01:05.56]Neon sleeping on my skin
[01:07.80]Afterglow, afterglow
[01:10.08]Let the quiet pull me in
[01:12.12]The bar is never closing now
[01:14.36]The street is shining after rain
[01:16.84]Afterglow, afterglow
[01:19.16]Say nothing, stay again
[01:41.12][Verse]
[01:41.20]Vending lights blink through the wetness
[01:45.16]Chrome reflections lose their face
[01:49.36]A stranger leaves a matchbook burning
[01:54.32]On the counter near my glass
[01:58.72]Midnight radio says traffic
[02:03.24]Far away a siren bends
[02:07.72]I don't ask the name behind me
[02:12.28]Names are where the evening ends
[02:16.00]The mirrors know the borrowed smiles
[02:20.52]The hotel hall remembers shoes
[02:25.28]Morning waits behind the billboard
[02:29.20]But the neon keeps its blue
[02:33.76]Afterglow, afterglow
[02:36.00]Neon sleeping on my skin
[02:38.24]Afterglow, afterglow
[02:40.56]Let the quiet pull me in
[02:42.56]The bar is never closing now
[02:44.84]The street is shining after rain
[02:47.32]Afterglow, afterglow
[02:49.56]Say nothing, stay again
